WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
- You look so beautiful!

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.780
- Oh my god you sounded so beautiful.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.137
How amazing was that?

00:00:06.137 --> 00:00:08.008
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.600
- Well, I was nervous
'cause you're here (laughs).

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.740
- Oh please.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.290
- But I was like, oh it might be cool,

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.170
they requested it and yeah we
knew you were gonna be here.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.090
- I've always loved your voice.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.390
- Oh my gosh ditto!

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.223
- She can blow.

00:00:17.223 --> 00:00:18.056
I love it
- Dude but singing your songs.

00:00:18.056 --> 00:00:20.240
I've also covered a few
of your songs on tour

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.030
like over the past 17 years or whatever

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.296
and your songs, girl, they are rangey!

00:00:24.296 --> 00:00:25.651
(laughing)

00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:26.934
Like I love it.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:27.767
(audience cheering)

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.680
It's rare, like not everybody has

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.240
that kind of range and power.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.800
- Well thank you, thank you.
- It's rare, yeah.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.618
- Yeah, I over-complicate
things for myself live.

00:00:36.618 --> 00:00:37.451
(laughs)
- Don't you hate that?

00:00:37.451 --> 00:00:38.850
And then you get to the
tour and you're like

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.940
why couldn't I just not do the octave.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.950
- I change it up a little bit.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.230
- You're touring right now, right?

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.460
- I am touring and, yeah,
I hadn't toured before that

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.630
in like 10 years 'cause I was --

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.430
- Why didn't you tour
for, is it 'cause kids?

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.870
- Yes I got really scared.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.625
I'm like how do people do this?

00:00:54.625 --> 00:00:56.650
'Cause I'm very, like I
know kids need like routine

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.230
and structure like bedtime,
the order and like,

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:00.230
how are you supposed to do that

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.540
whenever you're in different time zones

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.833
like every night and
things are changing, so.

00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:03.830
- It's so hard.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.740
- It was (laughs).
- Yeah.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.798
I cried when I first had River

00:01:06.798 --> 00:01:07.840
and then we had two older kids,

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:08.673
I cried
- It's hard!

00:01:08.673 --> 00:01:09.694
- Like almost every night.

00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:10.800
I was like this is so hard.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.633
- It's so hard.
- 'Cause you don't wanna

00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:12.550
be an absentee mom.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.590
- And then you're off stage

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.510
and it's like oh the bedtime stories, okay

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.500
what almost there to the, you know.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.400
- And they're like sing me a song

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.809
and I'm like I just did.

00:01:20.809 --> 00:01:21.710
(audience laughs)

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:22.700
You're welcome.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:23.590
- See I have it more easy.
- You didn't have

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:24.423
to pay for it.

00:01:24.423 --> 00:01:26.210
- I have it more easy 'cause
my daughter will be like

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.430
shh I'm trying to sleep.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.330
And I'm there like okay cool.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:30.370
- My daughter does that to me!

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:32.440
She also, she'll be like let's
sing and then she'll go shh.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.927
- Yes she does the hand to me too!

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.600
- I'm like people pay for this.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.495
- She gives me that hand, they don't know,

00:01:38.495 --> 00:01:39.328
they don't know.
- Yes, they shush you.

00:01:39.328 --> 00:01:40.710
They don't care , it's kind of awesome.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:41.810
- Yeah it's great.
- 'Cause it keeps us humble

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.880
our kids don't care at all.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.920
No I love you and I love that actually,

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.450
I feel like we have
similar childhoods speaking

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.350
about parenting and everything.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.260
Like I have like major abandonment issues

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:53.660
so like that's one reason why I am like

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.600
not a helicopter mom but I really wanna

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.433
be there for everything.
- Same I do too.

00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:57.680
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.040
- You had kind of a normal childhood

00:01:59.040 --> 00:01:59.873
but it was kind of hard, right?

00:01:59.873 --> 00:02:00.706
Y'all struggled a bit.

00:02:00.706 --> 00:02:02.070
- Yeah, it was a chaotic childhood

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.180
and lots of moving.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.450
We've moved a lot of different places.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.870
My dad was in the army so it
was like a lot of shifting

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.750
and people ask me like where are you from?

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.490
I'm like I was born in Staten Island

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.610
but I was raised everywhere, like Japan,

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:13.740
like everything, so--

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.860
- Japan?

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.910
- Yeah, Japan for three years.
- What?

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:18.743
- Yeah, so I just--

00:02:18.743 --> 00:02:19.576
- I love Japan.

00:02:19.576 --> 00:02:21.080
- It's, isn't it fun?

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.220
- I love Japan.
- It is so fun.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.022
Tokyo, so many things.
- It's so beautiful.

00:02:25.022 --> 00:02:26.340
- So many things, yeah.
- Yeah!

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:27.364
Oh my gosh

00:02:27.364 --> 00:02:28.243
that's so exciting!
- I keep forgetting

00:02:28.243 --> 00:02:29.660
to post pictures from it
but yeah, it was amazing.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:30.520
- Here's it, I know I like your life!

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.517
- I'm not a poster everybody was wow.

00:02:33.517 --> 00:02:36.129
- I'm not either 'cause
don't you feel like vain?

00:02:36.129 --> 00:02:37.651
Don't you feel it?
- I do!

00:02:37.651 --> 00:02:39.210
- Yeah I think so many egocentric!

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.980
- Well 'cause social media was not around

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.131
when I was--
- I'm so thankful!

00:02:43.131 --> 00:02:44.391
I'm so thankful!

00:02:44.391 --> 00:02:46.650
- Now it's kinda frightening
to think of where it's gonna be

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.620
when our kids are like--
- Yeah, I'm not even like

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.832
giving them phones.

00:02:49.832 --> 00:02:50.730
(audience laughs)

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.023
I'm like send a pigeon.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:53.773
- But yes, I did feel it at first.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.540
I was like what is this selfie,

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.700
like why do I want that in my face?

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:58.737
Like ah!
- I know!

00:02:58.737 --> 00:02:59.570
- Like you know what I mean?

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.920
- Yeah I feel like it's
like vanity run amuck,

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.820
but I know people get
into it, yeah I know.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.580
But one of the reasons why I loved,

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.440
and I have covered a lot of your songs,

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.250
honestly is because, for females,

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.920
you have such an amazing catalog,

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.880
like your empowerment level
of females especially,

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.080
it's so cool!

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.390
- Thank you.
- Yeah and I know,

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.890
I've just heard you speak
a little in interviews

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.370
here and there just 'cause of a fan,

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:21.000
and we both have a little bit
of an emotional upbringing

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:21.940
as well as financial,

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.870
and I think that's why it's so powerful,

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.981
when you sing those anthems--
- Thank you

00:03:25.981 --> 00:03:26.814
- Because you're so believable.

00:03:26.814 --> 00:03:28.370
- I appreciate that.
- I love your anthems.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.900
- Authenticity is very
important to me with my music.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.650
It's probably why I take so long to,

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.620
I can't just take a song and do it,

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.190
that's like regurgitating, not your truth.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.630
And I made a decision when
I made the Stripped album,

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.883
which was my follow up to my first--

00:03:41.883 --> 00:03:44.340
- Which was real good. I saw
that tour, it was so good!

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.365
In Dallas, in Dallas, I was like "Yes!"

00:03:47.365 --> 00:03:48.997
- With the chaps and the--
- It was so good!

00:03:48.997 --> 00:03:51.730
You say Eda James, and I was like yes!

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.125
(audience laughs)

00:03:53.125 --> 00:03:54.171
Yes, it was so good.

00:03:54.171 --> 00:03:55.940
- And what were we even talking about?

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.058
- I don't even know.

00:03:57.058 --> 00:03:58.933
(couple laughs)

00:03:58.933 --> 00:03:59.870
I was bragging about you,

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.070
'cause you know, you
give me chills and I--

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:07.070
- And the truth, I've always
wanted to be a truth seeker,

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.850
and I felt like that was really
important to my fans too,

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.010
after Stripped, I really told my truth,

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.240
and, you know, sides to
all woman that we are.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.690
You know, we shouldn't
be apologetic if we have,

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.720
for our sexual side,
for our vulnerable side,

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.530
through being a fighter
and overcoming obstacles.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.800
And I think those are all messages

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.284
that were really important to me.

00:04:27.284 --> 00:04:28.371
- That we're all different.

00:04:28.371 --> 00:04:29.732
(audience laughs)

00:04:29.732 --> 00:04:31.000
That's what I love about the industry too,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.120
is like even though we're all different,

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.360
there's room for everyone.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:36.037
There's room for everyone at the table.

00:04:36.037 --> 00:04:36.870
- Always, always.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:37.703
- And that's what I love about you too,

00:04:37.703 --> 00:04:39.320
you actually say, I know Demi's a big fan,

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.153
and y'all did that song together.

00:04:40.153 --> 00:04:41.030
- Yes!
- I love that.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.250
It was really really cool.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:43.083
But I have a question.

00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:45.050
So, when I'm on tour, I know that,

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.040
there's always like one
song that I'm still like

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:47.980
so excited about.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.490
Like I'm, funny enough, it's actually,

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.610
I had no idea, no one told
me at RCA, on my first label,

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:57.160
this is true, I got my record
and I was like oh my god,

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.410
my first record, and I'm like

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.450
sitting here looking at the booklet,

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.000
and I was like, why is
Christina Aguilera in it,

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.710
and I was like what?

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:06.100
And so you wrote, I didn't
know you wrote with Red,

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.497
the beginning of 'Miss Independent',

00:05:07.497 --> 00:05:08.865
like that part of that,
I didn't know that.

00:05:08.865 --> 00:05:10.423
- Oh that's right.

00:05:10.423 --> 00:05:11.368
- I had no idea.

00:05:11.368 --> 00:05:12.201
(audience cheers)

00:05:12.201 --> 00:05:14.520
I literally, no one told me.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.970
- I had no idea where
you were going with that.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.700
I was like, oh okay.
- No!

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.470
No because honestly no one told me

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.500
and I think this is the
thing that pissed me off,

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:22.810
'cause it's like why didn't you tell me,

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:23.970
'cause I love her.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.030
And I would have been so excited,

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.360
and what they told me is they were like,

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.480
well not all females love to
support all other females.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.340
And I was like, well
let's get rid of them.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.690
- That's messed up.
- Yeah, I--

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:36.150
- That's one of the
most discouraging things

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.480
I think about this business is
people definitely categorize

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.510
and pit you against each other,

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:43.136
when you have like even no idea.

00:05:43.136 --> 00:05:44.290
- Why don't they do that with males?

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.755
- So stupid.
- I know.

00:05:45.755 --> 00:05:46.737
(audience laughs)

00:05:46.737 --> 00:05:47.900
- We're changing it, we're changing it.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:49.087
- We're changing it!

00:05:49.087 --> 00:05:51.510
(audience cheers)

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.250
Is there a song that
you still love though,

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.120
like on your, like when you go on tour,

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.070
you're like oh my god I
can't wait to sing this.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:01.160
- Energetically what's super fun is

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.410
when the beginning opening
of 'Dirty' comes on.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.525
- I was hoping you would say 'Dirty'.

00:06:05.525 --> 00:06:07.187
I love that video.

00:06:07.187 --> 00:06:08.670
- And then, thank you,

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:11.570
and then the vulnerability
and the connection

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.270
that 'Beautiful' has with
people when I sing it,

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:17.910
it's such a relatable song
and such a truthful one too,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.750
you know, just expressing your
insecurities and being like,

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.080
well that's what I am,

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.245
and accepting yourself for it.
- Well and we all

00:06:24.245 --> 00:06:25.596
have insecurities, and we all have,

00:06:25.596 --> 00:06:27.660
it's funny, 'cause that's
why I wanted to do this show,

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:29.240
is that we all have far more commonalities

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.073
than differences,

00:06:30.073 --> 00:06:31.790
and that's one thing that I feel like

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.830
we should focus more on
because everybody is so divided

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.260
right now and I don't understand,

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.900
but anyway I have a couple a songs,

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.690
that if you want me to I'll mention,

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.123
I hate singing them on tour,

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.640
but what is one that you're like (groans)

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.067
like every time you get
on stage you're like,

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:46.883
"Good I get to do it again."

00:06:46.883 --> 00:06:48.520
(audience laughs)

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:50.320
Do you want me to go first
and make you feel better?

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.153
- Sure.

00:06:51.153 --> 00:06:52.970
- Okay, I don't know if you're
gonna feel bad about it.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.288
- Don't say 'Miss Independent.' (laughs)

00:06:55.288 --> 00:06:57.860
- No my band, my band is here,

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:58.930
like that's been with me forever.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.520
Is 'Miss Independent' not my favorite?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.430
I'm not kidding, it's
like super rocked out,

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:04.360
the version we do on tour,

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.600
and it's my favorite.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.430
And it was my first single, so funny.

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:09.490
But no the one, I think
because it wasn't for me,

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:12.370
do not hate me, do not
boo me, I will slap you.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:15.030
I won't slap you 'cause I
don't want you to sue me,

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.336
but (laughs), but it's,

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:19.300
'A Moment Like This' and only because,

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.600
don't you gasp!

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.730
But only because it wasn't written for me,

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.070
it was written for the winner.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.700
And so it could have been anybody's,

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:27.790
and so I feel like it wasn't,

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:28.780
like special for me.
- Okay,

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:30.830
that's fair enough.
- What's yours?

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:33.051
- Can I just say I really
love your set-up by the way.

00:07:33.051 --> 00:07:35.110
- Oh thank you.
- So comfy.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:37.530
I wish every talk show
had a set-up like this.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.350
- I did make sure, because of my height,

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:40.440
like we're both short,

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.980
I wanted pillows behind
people because I was--

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.635
- I know I love it!
- I'm like this.

00:07:43.635 --> 00:07:44.830
- Me too!

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.216
- Yeah.
- It's not fair!

00:07:46.216 --> 00:07:47.631
- It's not fun being short.

00:07:47.631 --> 00:07:49.230
- I feel like we're just
girlfriends gabbing right now.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.051
I don't even know if anybody's here.

00:07:51.051 --> 00:07:51.884
(laughs)

00:07:51.884 --> 00:07:53.848
What do I not like to sing...

00:07:53.848 --> 00:07:56.080
'Hurt', 'Hurt' is a big one.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.110
- 'Cause that's a big vocal.

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:58.282
- And it's all like all

00:07:58.282 --> 00:07:59.190
(Christina sings)

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:01.120
Like it's all extended vocals.
- Yep.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.650
